---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const services = [
  {
    id: 'fractional',
    label: '01',
    title: 'Fractional Executive Leadership',
    tagline: 'The executive your company needs — on the terms that make sense.',
    body: [
      'Building a high-growth company doesn\'t always mean carrying a full executive team on payroll. We provide fractional CEO, President, and Managing Director engagements that give growth-stage and mid-market companies access to seasoned, boardroom-ready leadership without the cost or commitment of a full-time hire.',
      'Our principals have held executive roles at Fortune-500-scale multinational operators. We embed directly into your organization — attending leadership meetings, managing cross-functional teams, running board-level reporting, and driving the strategic and operational decisions that move the needle.',
      'Engagements run on monthly retainers with milestone-based performance components. Scope is defined collaboratively: whether you need a CEO to lead a turnaround, a Managing Director to open a new market, or a transitional President while you run a search, we structure the engagement around your actual need.',
    ],
    scope: ['Strategic planning & OKR/KPI systems', 'Board-level governance and reporting', 'Operational turnaround and performance improvement', 'M&A preparation, integration oversight', 'Leadership team design and hiring', 'Investor and stakeholder management'],
  },
  {
    id: 'nearshoring',
    label: '02',
    title: 'US–Mexico Trade & Nearshoring Strategy',
    tagline: 'Navigate the US–Mexico corridor with executives who have lived it.',
    body: [
      'Nearshoring to Mexico is no longer a theoretical option — it\'s a strategic imperative for companies reassessing their supply chains, labor costs, and proximity to the US market. But executing a nearshoring strategy successfully requires more than a consultant with a framework. It requires operators who understand the regulatory, cultural, and commercial realities on both sides of the border.',
      'With over 12 years of senior leadership in US–Mexico cross-border operations, we advise companies at every stage of their nearshoring journey: from initial market assessment and site selection through binational organizational design, vendor and partner landscape mapping, and operational standup.',
      'We provide strategy and advisory services only. We do not offer logistics, freight, customs brokerage, warehousing, or fulfillment services of any kind.',
    ],
    scope: ['Market entry and feasibility analysis', 'Region and site selection advisory', 'Binational org design and talent strategy', 'Regulatory and trade compliance framework', 'Vendor and partner landscape mapping', 'Cross-border operating model design'],
  },
  {
    id: 'startup',
    label: '03',
    title: 'Startup & Venture Advisory',
    tagline: 'Build the operating system your startup needs to scale.',
    body: [
      'Early-stage companies move fast — but the ones that scale sustainably are those that build execution discipline early. We work with founders and early-stage leadership teams to install the operating frameworks that turn vision into traction: clear go-to-market strategy, org design that doesn\'t break at Series B, and the cadence systems (OKRs, KPIs, leadership rhythms) that keep a growing team aligned.',
      'Our advisory draws directly from senior leadership experience at global-scale operators. We know what good looks like at scale — and we help founders build toward it without prematurely over-engineering or under-building.',
      'We also support founders preparing for fundraising: narrative sharpening, financial model review, investor readiness, and diligence preparation. Not as bankers or lawyers — as operating advisors who have been in the room.',
    ],
    scope: ['Go-to-market strategy and channel design', 'Org design for growth-stage companies', 'OKR and KPI system design', 'Fundraising readiness and investor narrative', 'Leadership team coaching and development', 'Operating cadence and execution infrastructure'],
  },
  {
    id: 'ecommerce',
    label: '04',
    title: 'E-commerce & Cross-Border Commerce Strategy',
    tagline: 'Grow your brand across borders — strategically.',
    body: [
      'Selling into or out of Mexico and LATAM requires more than translating your website. It requires a deliberate market expansion strategy, an operating model built for cross-border complexity, and channel decisions grounded in how consumers actually shop in each market.',
      'We advise brands and operators on the strategic dimensions of cross-border commerce: market entry sequencing, channel strategy (marketplace vs. DTC vs. wholesale), operating model design for binational teams, and the commercial decisions that determine whether an expansion generates margin or destroys it.',
      'Our advisory is strictly strategic. We do not provide fulfillment, logistics, customs brokerage, or warehousing services.',
    ],
    scope: ['Market entry and expansion sequencing', 'Channel strategy (marketplace, DTC, B2B)', 'Cross-border operating model design', 'Pricing and margin strategy for new markets', 'Commercial partnerships and distributor strategy', 'Organizational design for multinational commerce'],
  },
  {
    id: 'ai',
    label: '05',
    title: 'Technology & AI Ventures',
    tagline: 'We build with AI — and we can help you do the same.',
    body: [
      'We don\'t advise on AI from the sidelines. We actively build and operate AI-native products and run our own firm using autonomous agents. That hands-on operating experience — being customer zero for the tools we build — is what separates our technology practice from conventional consulting.',
      'Our Technology & AI Ventures practice supports executives and operating companies navigating the AI inflection: from assessing where autonomous agents can generate real leverage in your workflows, to venture-building with AI-native methods, to evaluating and integrating AI tools at the executive level.',
      'This practice is also the foundation of PECH Labs — our applied-AI venture studio — where we design, deploy, and operate AI Agents as a Service for clients who want executive-grade automation without building it themselves.',
    ],
    scope: ['AI readiness assessment for operating companies', 'Autonomous agent workflow design', 'AI-native product strategy and venture-building', 'Executive AI literacy and adoption', 'Technology due diligence for investors', 'AI Agents as a Service (via PECH Labs)'],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Services"
  description="Five advisory practices: fractional executive leadership, US–Mexico nearshoring, startup advisory, cross-border commerce, and applied AI."
>

  <!-- Page Header -->
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section__label">Our Practices</span>
      <h1>Advisory built for<br/><span style="color:var(--gold)">the real work.</span></h1>
      <p class="page-header__sub">
        Five integrated practices. Deep cross-border expertise. Executive-level
        engagement — not slide decks.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Services -->
  {services.map((s, i) => (
    <section
      class={`service-section section ${i % 2 !== 0 ? 'section--off' : ''}`}
      id={s.id}
    >
      <div class="container service-section__inner">
        <div class="service-section__meta">
          <span class="service-num">{s.label}</span>
          <div class="gold-line"></div>
          <span class="section__label">{s.tagline}</span>
          <h2>{s.title}</h2>
          <ul class="scope-list">
            {s.scope.map(item => (
              <li>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary" style="margin-top:2rem;">Discuss This Practice</a>
        </div>
        <div class="service-section__body">
          {s.body.map(para => <p>{para}</p>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section" style="background: var(--navy);">
    <div class="container" style="text-align:center; max-width: 640px;">
      <span class="section__label" style="color:var(--gold)">Ready to engage?</span>
      <h2 style="color:var(--white); margin-bottom:1rem;">Let's talk about your situation.</h2>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6); margin-bottom:2rem;">
        We work with a select number of clients at a time. If there's a potential
        fit, we'd rather have a direct conversation than an intake form.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary">Start the Conversation</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: var(--navy);
    padding: 7rem 0 5rem;
  }
  .page-header h1 { color: var(--white); margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .page-header__sub {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .service-section__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .service-num {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 4rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--teal-ink); /* was gold @ 20% opacity: failed contrast */
    line-height: 1;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .service-section__meta h2 { margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem; font-size: 1.6rem; }

  .scope-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .scope-list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--slate);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .scope-list svg {
    width: 16px; height: 16px;
    stroke: var(--gold);
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 2.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .service-section__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
  .service-section__body p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .service-section__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  }
</style>
